Not so long ago there was a discussion about artifacts appearing on
a level.  I happened across Mjollnir in a shop in a game the other
day.  No, this wasn't a bones level.  Are artifacts supposed to appear
in shops?

I think it's a bad idea for the most potent weapon in the game to appear
in a shop on dungeon level 5.  It makes the game much too easy.  I'm
playing a wizard for once because I wanted to play with spells.  But with 
Mjollnir, there's no point in casting spells.  Hack 'n slash, even in 
the middle of a zoo, works fine.  I should probably stop whining about 
finding this weapon...

(Unfortunately I had already disposed of the shop keeper before finding
Mjollnir.  I'd like to know how much I would have been charged for it!)


